-- title:
--   Away units of the meet order R∩ sRs⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and work in the rational quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfying [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), i.e. $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $R$ is finitely generated; let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathbb{Z}$, and let $s\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$. Write $\hat{s}$ for the diagonal image of $s$ in $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}$ under [`Submodule.finiteIdeleDiagonal`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L43), and let $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R\,\hat{s}=R\sqcap\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,R\,\hat{s}$, the intersection of $R$ with the lattice of elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ lies in $\hat{s}\,\widehat{R}\,\hat{s}^{-1}$. For a lattice $\Lambda$, `awayUnits` $\Lambda\,v$ denotes the subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ cut out by intersecting, over all height-one primes $w\neq v$, the preimages under $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}\to(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w)^{\times}$ of the subgroup generated by those local units $u$ with both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ in the local box $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,w$. The assertion is the equality of subgroups of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ $$\mathrm{awayUnits}(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R\,\hat{s})\,v\;=\;\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R\,v\;\sqcap\;s\,(\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R\,v)\,s^{-1},$$ the second term being the image of $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R\,v$ under the inner automorphism $x\mapsto sxs^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic side of the level-raising step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary: the $v$-away unit group of the meet order $R\cap sRs^{-1}$ is exactly $\Gamma\cap s\Gamma s^{-1}$ for $\Gamma$ the $v$-away unit group of $R$. It is used in establishing the Atkin–Lehner relations between the level groups attached to a place in the coset-graph construction.
-- source:
